steps.step:
At the top of the IIFE body (after "use strict" if present) inject:
  const { guard } = window.ERPBootstrap.require("ERPGuard");
  if (!guard) return;

routeFileShape.template:
/** @requires ERPGuard */
(function () {
  const { guard } = window.ERPBootstrap.require("ERPGuard");
  if (!guard) return;

  /* optional: const $ = window.jQuery; */

  /* ── business logic only ──────────────────────────────────────────── */

  /* guard.error(message)                  ← was showErrorNow         */
  /* guard.scheduleInteractiveError(msg)   ← was scheduleInteractiveError */
  /* guard.getMsg("translation_key")       ← was getMsg(el, key)      */
  /* guard.getCsrfToken()                  ← was getToken()           */
  /* !guard.isInvalidUrl(url)              ← was verifyRoute(url)     */
})();

routeFileShape.bladePreservation:
Blade template literals embedded in JS strings MUST NOT be touched:
  {{route('name', [param])}}
  {{__('Translation string')}}
  {{$phpVariable}}
These are valid at Laravel compile time; the script must treat them
as opaque string content.
